.TH ROBOTEST-SUPERVISOR 8 "August 2026" "robotest-supervisor 0.1.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
robotest-supervisor \- bounded local process supervisor for RoboTest Lab
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robotest-supervisor
.RB [ \-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-check-config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robotest-supervisor
starts configured child process groups, monitors timestamped heartbeat files,
and applies a bounded exponential-backoff restart policy. It writes structured
events and an atomic status snapshot under its configured state directory.
.PP
The HTTP interface is read-only and binds exactly to 127.0.0.1. It exposes
.BR /healthz ,
.BR /readyz ,
.BR /v1/status ,
and
.BR /metrics .
There is no remote process-control endpoint.
.SH PACKAGED RUNTIME CONTRACT
The packaged stack child sets
.B ROBOTEST_RUNTIME_STATE_DIRECTORY
to the same canonical absolute directory as the configuration
.B state_directory
and publishes its heartbeat at
.IR state_directory /robotest-stack.heartbeat.
The startup wrapper derives
.IR state_directory /lifecycle-startup-result.json
from the same value. It accepts only an existing writable, non-symbolic-link
directory at or below
.IR /var/lib/robotest-supervisor ,
and rejects non-canonical paths and unsafe pre-existing derived files before
reading the ROS overlay.
.PP
The systemd unit confines the supervisor to CPUs 0 through 5. The wrapper also
uses
.BR taskset (1)
with
.B ROBOTEST_CPUSET
as a child-level defense. The wrapper publishes heartbeats from a separately
owned worker while it performs one bounded, signal-aware reap of the ROS launch
child. Cleanup also bounds and reaps an unresponsive heartbeat worker.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Read the strict versioned JSON configuration from
.IR path .
The default is
.IR /etc/robotest-supervisor/config.json .
.TP
.B \-check-config
Validate the configuration and exit without starting a child or HTTP server.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robotest-supervisor/config.json
Administrator configuration managed as a dpkg conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/events.jsonl
Prefix-retained structured lifecycle events.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/status.json
Atomically replaced current status.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/robotest-stack.heartbeat
Packaged stack heartbeat. Run-scoped configurations use the same basename
under their configured state directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/lifecycle-startup-result.json
Validated lifecycle startup result used to gate heartbeat publication. A
run-scoped wrapper uses the same basename under its runtime state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR taskset (1)
